{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"b42523ff0d5bf8fe","name":"card_unit_london_irish_rifles","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Britain/Homefront/units/card_unit_london_irish_rifles","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"LONDON IRISH RIFLES","text":"When you play a card with Bond, deal 1 damage to the enemy HQ.","flavorText":"The London Irish Rifles were formed in 1859 as a volunteer rifle corps in London, reflecting the city’s Irish community and military tradition. In WWII, the regiment expanded to two battalions under the Territorial Army. The 1st Battalion took part in the Battle of Graveney Marsh in 1940, the last recorded ground engagement with a foreign enemy on the British mainland. Both battalions were later deployed to the Mediterranean theater. They fought in Tunisia, joined the Allied landings in Sicily, and advanced through Italy. In 1944, they endured prolonged shelling and enemy counterattacks while holding a critical beachhead at Anzio. They later went on to help liberate Rome and fought through the Apennines into northern Italy. Throughout the campaign, the London Irish Rifles were noted for their combat effectiveness, earning a solid reputation within the 8th Army.","faction":"Britain","type":"infantry","rarity":"Uncommon","cost":2,"operationCost":1,"attack":2,"defense":4},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_unit_london_irish_rifles","title":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_unit_london_irish_rifles_title","SourceString":"LONDON IRISH RIFLES","LocalizedString":"LONDON IRISH RIFLES"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::infantry","attack":2,"defense":4,"range":1,"faction":"EFactionEnum::Britain","kredits":2,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_unit_london_irish_rifles_text","SourceString":"When you play a card with Bond, deal 1 damage to the enemy HQ.","LocalizedString":"When you play a card with Bond, deal 1 damage to the enemy HQ."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_unit_london_irish_rifles_history","SourceString":"The London Irish Rifles were formed in 1859 as a volunteer rifle corps in London, reflecting the city’s Irish community and military tradition. In WWII, the regiment expanded to two battalions under the Territorial Army. The 1st Battalion took part in the Battle of Graveney Marsh in 1940, the last recorded ground engagement with a foreign enemy on the British mainland. Both battalions were later deployed to the Mediterranean theater. They fought in Tunisia, joined the Allied landings in Sicily, and advanced through Italy. In 1944, they endured prolonged shelling and enemy counterattacks while holding a critical beachhead at Anzio. They later went on to help liberate Rome and fought through the Apennines into northern Italy. Throughout the campaign, the London Irish Rifles were noted for their combat effectiveness, earning a solid reputation within the 8th Army.","LocalizedString":"The London Irish Rifles were formed in 1859 as a volunteer rifle corps in London, reflecting the city’s Irish community and military tradition. In WWII, the regiment expanded to two battalions under the Territorial Army. The 1st Battalion took part in the Battle of Graveney Marsh in 1940, the last recorded ground engagement with a foreign enemy on the British mainland. Both battalions were later deployed to the Mediterranean theater. They fought in Tunisia, joined the Allied landings in Sicily, and advanced through Italy. In 1944, they endured prolonged shelling and enemy counterattacks while holding a critical beachhead at Anzio. They later went on to help liberate Rome and fought through the Apennines into northern Italy. Throughout the campaign, the London Irish Rifles were noted for their combat effectiveness, earning a solid reputation within the 8th Army."},"operationCost":1,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Uncommon","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::Homefront","EffectType":"ECardEffectTypes::Trigger","usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardPlayedFromHand"],"extraHelpText